This is a warning about a bug..errr..unlisted feature which I found in thisprogram. Say, for example you have two programs in the default directory formcvert (see ENV variables), named p & p.bin. Now according to the Docswhen you type: "mcvert -U p", it should be eqivalent to "mcvert -U p.bin",assuming the default extension is still '.bin' Unfortunately, it would appear that it tries to convert the file 'p' first, not p.bin. Well ifp is an OSK binary interesting things happen. Like it tries to fillyour HD with HQX files of the default length or the ENV variable length.Rather Nasty. Please be careful what you input, the system you save maybe your own!